From: PC110 Web <pc110-web@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] emscripten: avoid mismatched GLib length pointer on wasm32

On Emscripten wasm32, QEMU's size_t and GLib's gsize have equal widths but
different C typedefs. The procfs helper does not consume the returned length,
so omit it rather than passing an incompatible pointer.

---
 util/oslib-posix.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/util/oslib-posix.c b/util/oslib-posix.c
--- a/util/oslib-posix.c
+++ b/util/oslib-posix.c
@@ -696,9 +696,8 @@ char *qemu_get_pid_name(pid_t pid)
 #else
     /* Assume a system with reasonable procfs */
     char *pid_path;
-    size_t len;
 
     pid_path = g_strdup_printf("/proc/%d/cmdline", pid);
-    g_file_get_contents(pid_path, &name, &len, NULL);
+    g_file_get_contents(pid_path, &name, NULL, NULL);
     g_free(pid_path);
 #endif
